rec-status · edge gate            English | 中文: README.zh-CN
=======================

Cloudflare Turnstile for file.example.com (OpenList) and rec.example.com (the recorder WebUI).

Sitekey: YOUR_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY  (the widget's domains must include both hosts)

Host path /opt/1panel/www/common/turnstile  ==  /www/common/turnstile in the OpenResty container.


Files
-----
  secret          Turnstile secret key (root 600). Write it with set-secret.sh.
  cookie_key      random HMAC key for the session/share cookies (root 600).
  rec_auth        "user:pass" of the recorder's Basic auth (root 600). Write it with set-rec-auth.sh.
  rs_key          root 600; same value as the status site's ingest_key (see rs_verify.lua).
  turnstile.lua   Siteverify + cookie helpers.
  file_gate.lua   file.example.com: blocks /api/auth/login* without a valid X-Turnstile-Token.
                  SSO (2026-11-13; Microsoft sign-in used to skip Turnstile entirely):
                  /api/auth/sso?method=sso_get_token needs ?ts=<Turnstile token> (openlist.js
                  adds it to the popup URL) and Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin, then sets a signed
                  10-min cookie site_sso (Path=/api/auth/, MAC with cookie_key). The callbacks
                  (/api/auth/sso_callback, /get_sso_id, /sso_get_token) need that cookie; its
                  nonce is single-use (shared dict). method=get_sso_id (linking an account from
                  the profile page; returns no OpenList token) is exempt.
                  sso_compatibility_mode (full-page redirect) is NOT supported: it gets the
                  403 page, because openlist.js can only add the token to window.open().
  share_gate.lua  file.example.com share links (2026-11-16; they used to open with no check at all):
                  /@s/<id> pages, POST /api/fs/* whose JSON names a /@s path, and share downloads
                  (/sd/, plus /sp/ /sad/ /sap/ /sae/) need the site_share cookie (2 h, HMAC with
                  cookie_key, any share). Without it: /@s/ pages get templates/share_gate.html
                  (Turnstile, action openlist-share, auto-continues via public/share.js), /sd/
                  302s to the share page, API calls get OpenList-style {"code":403}. The check
                  POSTs to /__turnstile/share (same-origin only; only /@s/ return paths). Called
                  first thing from file_gate.lua. Downloads therefore need the browser that passed
                  the check (download managers without its cookie are sent to the share page).
  rs_verify.lua   POST /__turnstile/rs-verify (own location in sites/file.conf): Turnstile check for
                  rec-status.example.com's sign-in, called by that server. Signed: X-RS-Ts + X-RS-Sig =
                  hex HMAC-SHA1(rs_key, "rs-verify|ts|body"). Checks action rec-status and hostname
                  rec-status.example.com, single use. Reload after changing rs_key (it's cached).
  rec_auth.lua    rec.example.com: credential check, session cookie (site_rec), lockout.
  rec_gate.lua    rec.example.com: no valid session -> 302 to /__turnstile/login (401 JSON for
                  non-GET); valid session -> adds the recorder's Basic Authorization upstream.
                  Always strips the visitor's own Authorization header (2026-11-13: it let
                  /.well-known/* and /__turnstile* act as a password oracle, 401 vs 404).
                  Only /__turnstile/ and /.well-known/acme-challenge/ skip the session check.
  rec_login.lua   rec.example.com: GET/POST /__turnstile/login, IBM Carbon sign-in page.
                  POST checks Turnstile (action rec-login), then username/password.
  rec_logout.lua  rec.example.com: /__turnstile/logout clears the session.
  templates/      rec_login.html (rendered by rec_login.lua), share_gate.html (share check page).
                  Neither is served directly.
  public/         openlist.js (widget on the OpenList sign-in; also shows the cookie notice:
                  only necessary cookies, acknowledgement kept in localStorage
                  "site.cookie-notice"; the policy lives at https://rec-status.example.com/privacy,
                  source status-site/index/privacy.html), share.js + share.css (share check page).
  public/rec/     sign-in assets + the recorder theme (see "Recorder theme" below).
  tools/          build-carbon-css.py (not served), rec-theme-check/ (see "Recorder updates" below).
  sites/          nginx snippets: file.conf, rec.conf, siteverify.conf.


Activation
----------
One-line files (1Panel includes /www/sites/<site>/proxy/*.conf):
  /opt/1panel/www/sites/file.example.com/proxy/turnstile.conf -> include /www/common/turnstile/sites/file.conf;
  /opt/1panel/www/sites/rec.example.com/proxy/turnstile.conf  -> include /www/common/turnstile/sites/rec.conf;

Also required: /opt/1panel/www/conf.d/00-turnstile.conf (http level)
  lua_shared_dict site_turnstile 2m;   <- single-use token cache; Siteverify alone
                                          accepted a replayed token during testing.

Disable: delete those two proxy/turnstile.conf files and reload OpenResty.
  (rec.example.com then falls back to the recorder's own Basic prompt.)


rec.example.com sign-in (since 2026-11-10; replaced the Turnstile-only gate + browser Basic prompt)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Sessions: 12 h browser-session cookie, or 30 days with "Keep me signed in".
    The MAC covers rec_auth, so changing the recorder password signs everyone out.
  - 10 wrong passwords per client IP lock sign-in for 15 min (lua_shared_dict site_turnstile).
  - After changing BREC_HTTP_BASIC_PASS in /opt/1panel/docker/compose/rec, run
      /opt/1panel/www/common/turnstile/set-rec-auth.sh
    (copies it from the container env, checks it against the recorder, reloads).
  - Upstream WWW-Authenticate is hidden, so browsers never show a Basic prompt.
  - Sign out (public/rec/shell.js) is added to every recorder HTML page by sub_filter
    '</html>' in sites/rec.conf (header action on themed pages, floating button elsewhere).
    theme.css + shell.js are also added after <meta charset> on /, /ui/, /file/, /player/
    ($rec_theme). /file/ listings have no Content-Type, so a header_filter_by_lua_block in
    rec.conf labels them text/html for sub_filter. rec_gate.lua drops Accept-Encoding on
    HTML requests so sub_filter sees plain HTML; the WebUI's odd
    "text/html; encoding=utf-8" type is listed in sub_filter_types. Bump ?v= after edits.


Recorder theme (public/rec/)
----------------------------
  carbon.css      Carbon's compiled @carbon/styles 1.119.0 (Apache-2.0), trimmed to this page +
                  theme tokens; regenerate with tools/build-carbon-css.py from the "Carbon"
                  design-system artifact.
  rec.css         phones/tablets: centred card, 16px text, 56px fields. Desktop >= 66rem: photo
                  bg.jpg (placeholder; credit label .rec-credit) at 110% of screen height over a
                  blurred copy of itself; sign-in in a floating blurred-glass 26rem box on the
                  right, 48px fields; footer inside the box.
  login.js        password toggle, focus.   signout.js  (no longer referenced).
  logo.svg, fonts/  IBM Plex Sans 300/400/600 + Plex Mono 400 (fields), latin, OFL.
  Bump ASSET_V in rec_login.lua after editing anything here.

  theme.css + shell.js (2026-11-13): IBM Carbon theme for the recorder's own pages
  /, /ui/ (WebUI, Naive UI), /file/ and /player/. Nothing inside the recorder is changed.
    - theme.css re-points Naive UI's --n-* variables at Carbon tokens (White / Gray 100) and
      restyles the static pages.
    - shell.js sets data-rec-page / data-rec-theme before paint, adds a Gray 100 Carbon header
      (nav, light/dark switch, Sign out) to the static pages and puts Sign out in the WebUI
      header. Light/dark follows the WebUI's own switch (localStorage "brec.theme", dark by
      default); the static pages' switch writes the same key.
    - Other recorder pages (Swagger, GraphiQL ...) only get the floating Sign out button.
    - Bump ?v= in sites/rec.conf after editing either file.
    - Naive UI marks quaternary/tertiary buttons only in its theme-class hash
      (e.g. "__button-dark-dhlmmd"), so theme.css matches [class*="hl"] etc.; a WebUI upgrade
      could change that. Backup before: turnstile-backup-20261113-theme.


Recorder updates (tools/rec-theme-check/, added 2026-11-14)
-----------------------------------------------------------
  The theme lives here, not in the container, so pulling a new bililive/recorder image keeps it.
  What can break is the fit: theme.css relies on the WebUI's Naive UI markup.
  rec-theme-check.timer runs hourly; when rec-recorder-1 runs a new image it tests the theme
  against the new WebUI in a headless browser (check.py, image rec-theme-check:local built from
  the Dockerfile there). If it no longer fits it creates /www/common/turnstile/rec-theme.off and
  nginx (rec.conf) serves the recorder's original look; Sign out still works. A later passing
  check removes the file again.
    rec-theme-check.sh --status | --force      journalctl -u rec-theme-check


Origin lockdown (2026-11-13)
----------------------------
  Ports 80/443 accept only Cloudflare, loopback and Docker bridges (nftables table inet cf_origin,
  /usr/local/sbin/cf-origin-firewall.sh, systemd cf-origin-firewall.service + weekly
  -refresh.timer). So CF-Connecting-IP can be trusted, and nobody can skip Cloudflare Access by
  hitting 203.0.113.10 directly. Undo: cf-origin-firewall.sh off.


Notes
-----
  - openlist.js is injected as /__turnstile/openlist.js?v=N. Cloudflare and browsers cache .js
    for 4 h, so bump v= in sites/file.conf after editing the script.
  - OpenList's login page treats ANY window postMessage with a `token` field as an SSO login
    (no origin check). Turnstile's iframe posts such messages, so openlist.js hides messages
    from https://challenges.cloudflare.com from every listener except Turnstile's. Without that,
    the login page loops / -> /@login with "Token is invalidated".
  - WebDAV (/dav) and passkey logins do not go through Turnstile (passkey login is disabled).
  - After changing secret or cookie_key: reload OpenResty
      sudo docker exec 1Panel-openresty-XXXX openresty -s reload
  - Rejections are logged (level error) in each site's log/error.log ("turnstile:").
